                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Not quite Yes, rather Maybe\n\nYou just go forward and bash bad guys over the head - that's literally the whole gameplay. But the bad guys won't just stand there, they hit you back, and that's where the difficulty comes from. A Bastard's Tale is a damn hard game, it demands your full focus and understanding of its mechanics. Despite the simple game design, it's worth beating at least once - it'll give you a ton of emotions\n\nPast the first playthrough (I'm talking NG++ and endless mode), the game isn't really about skill anymore - it's about dumb luck",
